Now I have a comprehensive picture. Here is the full analysis:

---

## Complete Theme/Color CSS Analysis

### 1. How Light/Dark Themes Are Implemented

The theming system uses three mechanisms working together:

**A. `data-webtui-theme` attribute on `<html>` (primary method)**

The layout file sets the initial theme at load time:

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/web/src/layouts/Layout.astro` (lines 6, 11-21)
- The HTML element starts with `data-webtui-theme="light"` as the default.
- An inline `<script>` immediately reads `localStorage.getItem('webtui-theme')` and falls back to `window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` to pick `'dark'` or `'light'`, then sets `data-webtui-theme` on `document.documentElement`.

**B. `:root` defaults and `[data-webtui-theme]` overrides**

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/css/src/base.css`
- `:root` defines light-mode defaults (`--background0: #fff`, `--foreground0: #000`, etc.)
- `[data-webtui-theme='dark']` overrides them to dark values (`--background0: #1c1c1c`, `--foreground0: #fff`, etc.)

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/web/src/styles/themes/custom.css` (lines 345-494)
- `[data-webtui-theme='light']` block: sets `--oklch-scale: 0.85`, all semantic colors (`--red`, `--green`, `--blue`, etc.), heading colors (`--h1` through `--h6`), accent, url, code-bg, background/foreground tiers, and Catppuccin-like palette values for light mode.
- `[data-webtui-theme='dark']` block: sets `--oklch-scale: 1.15`, dark heading colors (using Material Design palette variables like `--material-pink-200`), accent/url/code-bg, background/foreground tiers, and a full Catppuccin Macchiato palette (rosewater through lavender).

**C. `prefers-color-scheme` media query**

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/web/src/styles/global.css` (lines 516-544)
- Used only for `.light-content` / `.dark-content` display toggling (showing/hiding content based on theme).
- Also has explicit `html[data-webtui-theme='light']` and `html[data-webtui-theme='dark']` overrides for the same `.light-content` / `.dark-content` classes.

---

### 2. Catppuccin Color Variables Available

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-catppuccin/src/base.css`

Four flavors are defined, each providing these **27 variables**:

| Variable | Mocha | Macchiato | Frappe | Latte |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `--rosewater` | `#f5e0dc` | `#f4dbd6` | `#f2d5cf` | `#dc8a78` |
| `--flamingo` | `#f2cdcd` | `#f0c6c6` | `#eebebe` | `#dd7878` |
| `--pink` | `#f5c2e7` | `#f5bde6` | `#f4b8e4` | `#ea76cb` |
