The selectors for each flavor:
- `[data-webtui-theme='catppuccin']` or `[data-webtui-theme='catppuccin-mocha']` -- Mocha (default)
- `[data-webtui-theme='catppuccin-macchiato']`
- `[data-webtui-theme='catppuccin-frappe']`
- `[data-webtui-theme='catppuccin-latte']`

All four flavors share a common semantic mapping (line 120-129, using `[data-webtui-theme|='catppuccin']`):
```css
--background0: var(--base);
--background1: var(--surface0);
--background2: var(--surface1);
--background3: var(--surface2);
--foreground0: var(--text);
--foreground1: var(--subtext1);
--foreground2: var(--overlay2);
```

Additionally, in `custom.css` `[data-webtui-theme='dark']` (lines 471-484), the Catppuccin Macchiato palette is embedded directly into the generic dark theme, providing rosewater through lavender at the custom-theme level.

---

### 3. Theme CSS Files in `packages/`

There are **5 theme packages**, each with identical structure:

| Package | Directory | Selector Prefix |
|---|---|---|
| **Catppuccin** | `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-catppuccin/src/` | `[data-webtui-theme\|='catppuccin']` |
| **Nord** | `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-nord/src/` | `[data-webtui-theme='nord']` |
| **Gruvbox** | `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-gruvbox/src/` | `[data-webtui-theme\|='gruvbox']` |
| **Vitesse** | `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-vitesse/src/` | `[data-webtui-theme\|='vitesse']` |
| **Everforest** | `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-everforest/src/` | `[data-webtui-theme\|='everforest']` |

Each has the same file layout:
```
src/
  index.css          -- imports base.css + components/*
  base.css           -- @layer base { color variable definitions }
  components/
    badge.css        -- @layer components { badge variant colors }
    button.css       -- @layer components { button variant colors }
    typography.css   -- @layer components { heading/link/code colors }
```

There is also a site-local custom theme:
- `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/web/src/styles/themes/custom.css` -- `:root` material design palette + `[data-webtui-theme='light']` and `[data-webtui-theme='dark']` definitions
- `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/web/src/styles/themes/terminaldotshop.css` -- a novelty theme with brand-specific badge variants

---

### 4. Badge Component Styling and `variant-` Attributes

**Base badge component:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/css/src/components/badge.css`

The badge uses the custom attribute selector `[is-~='badge']` and is entirely driven by two CSS variables: `--badge-color` and `--badge-text`.

**Core rendering:**
- Uses `background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, ...)` to create a colored band that leaves 1ch transparent gutters on each side.
- `::before` and `::after` pseudo-elements are 1ch-wide blocks filled with `--badge-color` to create the end caps.
- Height is `1lh`, display is `inline-flex`.

**Built-in `variant-` values** (from base `badge.css`):
- `variant-='foreground0'` (also the default when no `variant-` is present)
- `variant-='foreground1'`
- `variant-='foreground2'`
- `variant-='background0'`
- `variant-='background1'`
- `variant-='background2'`
- `variant-='background3'`

**Cap styles** via `cap-` attribute (with `^` for start, `$` for end):
- `cap-^='round'` / `cap-$='round'` -- rounded end caps via `border-radius: 1lh`
- `cap-^='triangle'` / `cap-$='triangle'` -- arrow-point clip-path
- `cap-^='slant-top'` / `cap-$='slant-top'` -- diagonal slant (top)
- `cap-^='slant-bottom'` / `cap-$='slant-bottom'` -- diagonal slant (bottom)
- `cap-^='ribbon'` / `cap-$='ribbon'` -- chevron/ribbon notch clip-path

**Theme-specific badge variants** add color-named variants:

- **Catppuccin** (`/packages/theme-catppuccin/src/components/badge.css`): 14 variants -- `rosewater`, `flamingo`, `pink`, `mauve`, `red`, `maroon`, `peach`, `yellow`, `green`, `teal`, `sky`, `sapphire`, `blue`, `lavender`
- **Vitesse** (`/packages/theme-vitesse/src/components/badge.css`): 8 variants -- `red`, `green`, `yellow`, `blue`, `purple`, `aqua`, `orange`, `gray`
- **Everforest** (`/packages/theme-everforest/src/components/badge.css`): 7 variants -- `red`, `green`, `yellow`, `blue`, `purple`, `aqua`, `orange`
- **Gruvbox** (`/packages/theme-gruvbox/src/components/badge.css`): 8 variants -- `red`, `green`, `yellow`, `blue`, `purple`, `aqua`, `orange`, `gray`
- **Nord** (`/packages/theme-nord/src/components/badge.css`): 15 variants -- `nord0` through `nord15` (each mapping to the corresponding `--nordN` variable)
- **terminaldotshop** (`/web/src/styles/themes/terminaldotshop.css`): 7 variants -- `brand`, `artisan`, `object-object`, `segfault`, `dark-mode`, `404`, `cron`

---

### 5. Statusline-Specific CSS Variables

Only the **Everforest** theme defines `--statusline` variables:

**File:** `/Users/samforeman/projects/saforem2/sam.onl/packages/theme-everforest/src/base.css`

```css
/* Dark (line 12-14) */
[data-webtui-theme|='everforest-dark'] {
    --statusline1: #a7c080;   /* green */
    --statusline2: #d3c6aa;   /* fg/neutral */
    --statusline3: #e67e80;   /* red */
}

/* Light (line 76-78) */
[data-webtui-theme|='everforest-light'] {
    --statusline1: #93b259;   /* green */
    --statusline2: #708089;   /* gray */
    --statusline3: #e66868;   /* red */
}
```

No other theme package or custom CSS file defines `--statusline1`, `--statusline2`, or `--statusline3`.

---

